B.aiy=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that convert a long trend description into a grounded analytical question.",B.M3,"The failure mode is confident storytelling. Lock measurement fields and force assumptions to validate so analysis stays real.","Rewrite into one analytical question. Identify metric + timeframe (mark [Unknown] if missing). Require segmentation (category/source). No invented causes. Output one question + 3 assumptions to validate.","You\u2019re now asking analysis questions the model can answer without hallucinating a narrative.","Rewrite the description into one analytical question. Identify the metric and timeframe (mark [Unknown] if missing). Require segmentation (category/source) to find drivers. Do not invent causes. Output: one question plus three assumptions to validate first.")
B.a9R=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *measurement discipline*.\n- Requirements forced metric + timeframe and banned invented causes\n- Expectations required assumptions to validate, preventing false certainty\n- Objective kept the question analytical (segment drivers) instead of narrative")
B.acw=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nTurn this into a question about the trend\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite into one analytical question. Identify metric + timeframe (mark [Unknown] if missing). Require segmentation (category/source). No invented causes. Output one question + 3 assumptions to validate.")
B.ac1=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nTrend description with mixed certainty\n\nO - Objective\nAI-ready analytical question that guides analysis\n\nR - Requirements\nMetric + timeframe; segmentation; no invention\n\nE - Expectations\nOne question + 3 assumptions to validate")
B.MH=s([B.a9R,B.acw,B.ac1],t.c)
B.adg=new A.ab("Turn a long data description into a simple analytical question","You get a long explanation about recent trends.\n\nIt mixes observations, guesses, and emotions\u2014so nobody is sure what to investigate.\n\nIf you ask AI \u201cwhy is this happening?\u201d, it will invent a story.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - trend description with mixed certainty\n- Objective - turn it into an AI-ready analytical question\n- Requirements - identify metric, timeframe, segmentation, and what decision it should inform\n- Expectations - one question + assumptions to validate","Rewrite the description into one analytical question.\n\nRequirements:\n- Identify the metric and timeframe; if missing, mark [Unknown]\n- Ask for a segmented view (e.g., category/source) rather than one global answer\n- Do not invent causes\n- Output:\n  1) One analytical question\n  2) 3 assumptions we must validate first\n\nReturn only the output.","**Analytical question**\nWhy have support tickets increased this month, and which categories are contributing most to the rise?\n\n**Assumptions to validate (first)**\n- Which ticket categories and channels are included in \u201csupport tickets\u201d? [Unknown]\n- Is the increase absolute volume, rate per customer, or backlog growth? [Unknown]\n- Did ticket tagging or routing change this month (measurement shift)? [Unknown]\n\nNotice how the prompt prevents story-time: it forces segmentation and \u201cassumptions to validate\u201d so the analysis stays grounded.","Analytical questions start with measurement integrity.","Trends lie when the measurement changed. Force \u201cassumptions to validate\u201d or the model will confidently explain a spike that\u2019s just tagging drift.",B.aiy,B.MH)
B.a47=new A.b("Specify metric and timeframe (mark [Unknown] if missing)",!0)
B.Zl=new A.b("Require segmentation by at least 2 dimensions",!0)
B.ZU=new A.b("Request 3 candidate explanations (not one cause)",!0)
B.a4i=new A.b("Require evidence needed to test each candidate",!0)
B.Tr=new A.b("Prohibit claiming a single definitive cause",!0)
B.Uk=new A.b("Remove unknowns to make it decisive",!1)
B.UB=new A.b("Ask for general best practices for conversion",!1)
B.a6C=new A.b("Request a narrative summary paragraph",!1)
B.a6l=new A.b("Ask for solutions without analysis",!1)
B.Ns=s([B.a47,B.Zl,B.ZU,B.a4i,B.Tr,B.yE,B.Uk,B.UB,B.a6C,B.a6l],t.W)
B.aiR=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that turn raw metrics into a hypothesis-and-evidence analytical question.",B.Ns,"Your goal is not a \u201cwhy story.\u201d It\u2019s a testable plan. Force candidates + evidence so the output stays honest and useful.","Turn these metrics into one analytical question. Include metric/timeframe (mark [Unknown] if missing). Require segmentation by 2+ dimensions. Ask for 3 candidate explanations and the evidence to test each. Don\u2019t claim one cause.","You\u2019re now prompting for investigation instead of narration\u2014this is where you gain an advantage over most AI users.","Turn the metrics into one analytical question. Specify the metric and timeframe (mark [Unknown] if missing). Require segmentation by at least two dimensions. Request three candidate explanations and the evidence needed to test each. Do not claim a single definitive cause.")
B.aad=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *hypothesis discipline*.\n- Requirements forced segmentation and banned single-cause claims\n- Expectations demanded candidates plus evidence, turning AI into an analysis planner\n- Objective preserved uncertainty while still creating actionability")
B.ab7=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nWhy did conversion change?\n\nStrong prompt:\nTurn metrics into one analytical question: specify metric/timeframe (mark unknowns), require segmentation by 2+ dimensions, request 3 candidate explanations and the evidence needed to test each. Don\u2019t claim a single cause.")
B.ac5=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nMetrics without an agreed hypothesis\n\nO - Objective\nActionable analysis without fake certainty\n\nR - Requirements\nMetric/timeframe; segmentation; 3 candidates + evidence; no single-cause claim\n\nE - Expectations\nOne question + candidate/evidence list")
B.MX=s([B.aad,B.ab7,B.ac5],t.c)
B.adR=new A.ab("Turn metrics into a clear question","You\u2019re given numbers (traffic, conversion, revenue), but nobody agrees what they mean.\n\nIf you ask \u201cwhy did conversion drop?\u201d, the model will guess.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - metrics without an agreed hypothesis\n- Objective - ask for an analysis that separates measurement, mix, and behaviour\n- Requirements - define metric, timeframe, segments; request candidate explanations *and* what evidence would support them\n- Expectations - one question + analysis plan","Turn the metrics into one clear analytical question.\n\nRequirements:\n- Specify metric + timeframe; mark missing as [Unknown]\n- Ask for segmentation by at least 2 dimensions (e.g., channel, device, region)\n- Ask for 3 candidate explanations *and* the evidence needed to test each\n- Do not claim a single cause\n\nReturn only one question followed by the 3 candidates with evidence.","**Analytical question**\nGiven the change in conversion over the last period [Unknown timeframe], which segments (channel, device, region) are driving the shift, and what are the top candidate explanations with the evidence needed to test each?\n\n**Candidates (with evidence to test)**\n1) Traffic mix shift (more low-intent traffic)\n   - Evidence: channel-level conversion changes; new campaign/source mix [Unknown]\n2) UX/performance regression in a segment\n   - Evidence: device/browser conversion drop; page load changes; error rates [Unknown]\n3) Measurement/attribution change\n   - Evidence: tracking changes; attribution model updates; event drop-offs [Unknown]\n\nThis is where you can see expert control: the prompt forces \u201ccandidates + evidence,\u201d so AI can\u2019t collapse uncertainty into a single story.","Expert analysis prompts force evidence, not certainty.","If you ask \u201cwhy,\u201d you get stories. If you ask for \u201ccandidates + evidence,\u201d you get investigation. That\u2019s the difference between analysis and narration.",B.aiR,B.MX)
B.YC=new A.b("Require one investigative question (not a conclusion)",!0)
B.Sj=new A.b("Convert vague terms into measurable metric definitions",!0)
B.a6q=new A.b("Ask which segments to analyse first",!0)
B.YV=new A.b("Provide 3 candidate metric definitions to choose from",!0)
B.a_q=new A.b("Ask AI to diagnose the root cause immediately",!1)
B.a2b=new A.b("Assume the issue is customer service",!1)
