B.a_i=new A.b("Request a motivational summary for stakeholders",!1)
B.VI=new A.b("Ask for solutions without measurement",!1)
B.Ky=s([B.YC,B.Sj,B.a6q,B.f3,B.YV,B.a_q,B.a2b,B.a3e,B.a_i,B.VI],t.W)
B.aj5=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that convert vague performance language into a measurable investigative question.",B.Ky,"Your advantage is refusing to \u201canalyse vibes.\u201d Force metric definitions and segmentation so the output becomes a real investigation plan.","Rewrite into one investigative question. Convert vague terms into measurable metric definitions as options. Ask which metric and segments to examine first. Don\u2019t invent causes. Output one question + 3 metric definition options.","You\u2019re now turning vague complaints into measurable investigations\u2014this is expert-level ambiguity control.","Rewrite the description into one precise investigative question. Convert vague terms into measurable metric definitions (as options). Ask which metrics and segments to examine first. Do not invent causes. Output: one question plus three candidate metric definitions.")
B.abd=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *measurability*.\n- Requirements forced vague words into metric definitions\n- Expectations produced options rather than pretending there\u2019s one metric\n- Objective prevented the model from inventing \u201cthe metric\u201d and then explaining it")
B.a99=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nTurn this into a precise question\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite into one investigative question. Convert vague terms into measurable metric definitions as options. Ask which metric and segments to examine first. Don\u2019t invent causes. Output one question + 3 candidate metric definitions.")
B.a8i=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nQualitative signals without agreed measurement\n\nO - Objective\nTurn into a measurable investigation\n\nR - Requirements\nDefine vague terms as metrics; segmentation; no invented causes\n\nE - Expectations\nOne question + 3 candidate metric definitions")
B.Ir=s([B.abd,B.a99,B.a8i],t.c)
B.adY=new A.ab("Turn unclear performance descriptions into precise questions","You get a vague performance description: \u201cit\u2019s worse lately,\u201d \u201ccustomers are unhappy,\u201d \u201cquality is down.\u201d\n\nIf you ask AI to analyse it as-is, it will invent metrics and causes.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - qualitative signals without measurement\n- Objective - turn into a measurable investigative question\n- Requirements - define what \u201cworse\u201d could mean; request measurement and segmentation; no invention\n- Expectations - one question + measurement definitions","Rewrite the description into a precise investigative question.\n\nRequirements:\n- Convert vague terms (\u201cworse,\u201d \u201cunhappy,\u201d \u201cquality down\u201d) into measurable definitions as options\n- Ask what metric(s) and segments we should examine first\n- Do not invent causes\n- Output:\n  1) One investigative question\n  2) 3 candidate metric definitions we should choose from\n\nReturn only the output.","**Investigative question**\nWhat specific metric indicates performance has worsened, and which segments should we analyse first to determine where the decline is concentrated?\n\n**Candidate metric definitions (choose one)**\n- Customer experience: complaint rate, CSAT/NPS change, support ticket volume per user [Unknown]\n- Product quality: defect rate, return/rework rate, incident frequency [Unknown]\n- Delivery performance: cycle time, on-time rate, backlog growth [Unknown]\n\nWhat matters here is measurement-first thinking: the prompt forces definitions so the model can\u2019t \u201canalyse\u201d a feeling as if it were data.","Measurement is the gateway to root-cause thinking.","The model can\u2019t analyse what you haven\u2019t defined. If you don\u2019t force metric definitions, you\u2019ll get confident analysis of an undefined problem.",B.aj5,B.Ir)
B.No=s([B.adg,B.adR,B.adY],t.r)
B.H3=new A.bR("Turn Data Descriptions Into Questions AI Can Answer",B.No,null)
