B.aiB=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that make tone friendlier without becoming casual or over-apologetic.",B.MQ,"Warmth that invents accountability is expensive. Specify acknowledgement + boundaries so the model can\u2019t \u201cpeople-please\u201d its way into risk.","Rewrite to be friendlier but still professional. Preserve meaning. Add one brief acknowledgement (no over-apology). Max 3 sentences. No slang or emojis. Return only the rewrite.","You\u2019ve learned to add warmth without creating liability\u2014most users over-correct and lose control.","Rewrite in a friendlier but still professional tone. Preserve meaning. Add one brief acknowledgement (no over-apology). Keep to max 3 sentences. No slang/emojis. Return only the rewritten message.")
B.a9_=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *warmth without liability*.\n- Requirements prevented over-apology and casual drift\n- Expectations capped length so warmth didn\u2019t become fluff\n- Objective kept the message professional while still human")
B.acv=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nMake this friendlier\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite to be friendlier while staying professional. Preserve meaning; add one brief acknowledgement (no over-apology); max 3 sentences; no slang/emojis. Return only the rewritten message.")
B.aaK=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nRelationship-sensitive reply that may be forwarded\n\nO - Objective\nIncrease warmth without lowering professionalism\n\nR - Requirements\nPreserve meaning; one acknowledgement line; concise; no casual drift\n\nE - Expectations\nMax 3 sentences, paste-ready")
B.Jx=s([B.a9_,B.acv,B.aaK],t.c)
B.ada=new A.ab("Rewrite for a Friendlier Tone","You need to respond to someone who feels ignored.\n\nYour current draft is correct, but it reads cold\u2014and the relationship cost will show up later.\n\nIf you over-correct, you can sound overly casual or apologetic for things you didn\u2019t do.\n\nIf you prompt AI weakly, it usually:\n- adds fake warmth (\u201chope you\u2019re well\u201d) that feels off\n- over-apologises and creates liability\n- becomes informal and loses credibility\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - relationship-sensitive reply\n- Objective - warmer tone without lowering professional standards\n- Requirements - acknowledge, clarify next step, keep boundaries\n- Expectations - short, paste-ready response","Rewrite the message to be friendlier while staying professional.\n\nRequirements:\n- Preserve meaning\n- Add one brief acknowledgement line (no over-apology)\n- Keep it concise (max 3 sentences)\n- Do not add casual slang or emojis\n\nReturn only the rewritten message.","Thanks for checking in \u2014 I appreciate the nudge. I'm reviewing the document now and will send the updated version shortly. If there\u2019s a specific section you want prioritised, tell me and I\u2019ll start there.\n\nPay attention to how tone stays warm without surrendering control: the prompt forced acknowledgement *and* boundaries.","Friendly tone is a constraint problem, not a personality problem.","If you don\u2019t say \u201cno over-apology,\u201d the model will invent accountability to sound nice. That\u2019s not friendliness\u2014that\u2019s risk.",B.aiB,B.Jx)
B.KI=s([B.adu,B.adm,B.ada],t.r)
