B.ai6=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that iterate roadmaps toward choices.",B.Lj,"Roadmap iteration is C.O.R.E. under scarcity: Requirements force the painful cuts.","Roadmap: PASS1 5 themes; PASS2 cut 1 + trade-off; PASS3 quarterly sequence + rationale; [Unknown] rev links.","You graduated from listing themes to owning sequencing\u2014iteration with teeth.","Iteratively refine a roadmap for a developer tool. Pass 1 lists five strategic themes. Pass 2 removes one theme and explains the trade-off in two bullets. Pass 3 sequences the remaining four themes across four quarters with a one-line rationale each, without inventing revenue impact\u2014use [Unknown] when needed. Label outputs PASS1, PASS2, and PASS3.")
B.abT=new A.k("What Made This Work","Cuts and sequencing appeared because passes had explicit jobs.\n- Context implied capacity tension\n- Objective moved from list \u2192 choice \u2192 timeline\n- Requirements forced a theme death and honest [Unknown] business links\n- Expectations made diffs visible pass to pass")
B.a9p=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nImprove this roadmap\n\nStrong prompt:\n5 themes; pass2 cut one w/ trade-off; pass3 quarterly sequence w/ rationale; [Unknown] revenue.")
B.acc=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nDeveloper tool; competing priorities\n\nO - Objective\nRefine roadmap across iterations\n\nR - Requirements\nExplicit cut + sequencing rules\n\nE - Expectations\nLabeled passes with before/after")
B.Jm=s([B.abT,B.a9p,B.acc],t.c)
B.adW=new A.ab("Roadmap themes: breadth, trade-offs, sequencing","Roadmaps lie when everything is \u201cP0.\u201d\n\nIteration can force trade-offs and order.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - capacity and customer pressure\n- Objective - refine themes across three iterations\n- Requirements - pass 2 must cut one theme; pass 3 must sequence what ships first with rationale\n- Expectations - show before/after each pass","Start with 5 roadmap themes for a developer tool.\n\nPass 1: brainstorm themes (list 5).\nPass 2: cut one theme and explain trade-off in 2 bullets.\nPass 3: sequence remaining 4 into Q1\u2013Q4 suggestion with one-line rationale each; no invented revenue impact\u2014use [Unknown].\n\nExpectations: label PASS1/PASS2/PASS3.","PASS1\n1) Reliability hardening\n2) New IDE integrations\n3) Enterprise SSO polish\n4) Usage-based billing\n5) Community templates marketplace\n\nPASS2\nCut: Community templates marketplace\n- Trade-off: slower ecosystem growth vs focus on revenue-critical features\n- Gain: frees eng for billing + SSO\n\nPASS3\nQ1 Reliability \u2014 unblocks enterprise deals [Unknown]\nQ2 SSO polish \u2014 removes security blockers in pipeline [Unknown]\nQ3 Billing \u2014 unlocks expansion revenue experiments [Unknown]\nQ4 IDE integrations \u2014 acquisition feature parity [Unknown]\n\nIteration turned a wishlist into a sequence with visible cuts.","Iteration without forced trade-offs is just formatting.","If pass 2 does not hurt, you are not prioritizing\u2014you are decorating.",B.ai6,B.Jm)
