B.a2L=new A.b("Add an emotional tone to increase urgency",!1)
B.Nb=s([B.a1l,B.a4C,B.Za,B.a5s,B.V2,B.a2E,B.a1z,B.WE,B.YF,B.a2L],t.W)
B.aiZ=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that turn a messy description into an investigable question without invented causes.",B.Nb,"Your advantage here is refusing fake certainty. Force \u201cinvestigable question + next clarifiers\u201d so the model can\u2019t hallucinate the analysis.","Rewrite into one investigable question. Preserve core problem + insight needed. No invented causes/solutions. Include scope/timeframe; if missing mark [Unknown]. Output one question + 3 clarifying questions.","You now turn messy reality into an investigation instead of a debate\u2014most people skip this and get generic answers.","Rewrite the description into one investigable question. Preserve the core problem and the insight needed. Do not invent root causes or solutions. Include timeframe/scope if stated; otherwise mark [Unknown]. Output: (1) one clear question, (2) three clarifying questions needed next.")
B.aa9=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *investigability*.\n- Requirements banned invented causes/solutions\n- Expectations forced two outputs: one question + the next clarifiers\n- Objective kept the work real: you\u2019re defining the investigation, not writing a recommendation")
B.abA=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nTurn this into a clear question\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite into a single investigable question. Preserve the core problem and insight needed. Don\u2019t invent root causes or solutions. Include timeframe/scope if stated; otherwise mark [Unknown]. Output: (1) one question, (2) 3 clarifying questions needed next.")
B.aaM=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nMessy description with competing narratives\n\nO - Objective\nOne investigable question that guides analysis\n\nR - Requirements\nPreserve core problem + desired insight; no invention; [Unknown] for missing scope\n\nE - Expectations\nOne clear question + 3 clarifying questions (next)")
B.M6=s([B.aa9,B.abA,B.aaM],t.c)
B.aeG=new A.ab("Turn a messy problem description into a clear AI question","You have a long, disorganised description of a process issue.\n\nMultiple people are blaming different steps, and the \u201cproblem\u201d keeps shifting depending on who you ask.\n\nIf you ask AI a vague question, you\u2019ll get a vague answer\u2014then everyone argues about the output instead of investigating.\n\nWeak prompting usually:\n- turns noise into a generic \u201chow to improve\u201d answer\n- invents likely causes to sound confident\n- collapses competing narratives into one neat story\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - messy description with competing viewpoints\n- Objective - produce one investigable question\n- Requirements - keep the core problem, timeframe, and target insight; no invented causes\n- Expectations - one question + a short list of clarifying questions needed next","Rewrite the description into a single, investigable question.\n\nRequirements:\n- Preserve the core problem and the insight needed\n- Do not invent root causes or solutions\n- Include the timeframe/scope if stated; if missing, mark it [Unknown]\n- Output format:\n  1) One clear question\n  2) 3 clarifying questions we must answer next\n\nReturn only the output in that format.","**Investigable question**\nWhat is causing the delay in the approval workflow, and which specific step should we focus on first to reduce end-to-end processing time?\n\n**Clarifying questions (next)**\n- Which step(s) show the longest wait time vs active work time? [Unknown]\n- Is the delay consistent or concentrated during specific periods (e.g., peak hours, end-of-month)? [Unknown]\n- Are delays driven by policy/criteria, tooling, or handoffs between roles? [Unknown]\n\nWhat matters here is disciplined ambiguity: the prompt bans invented causes and forces \u201cwhat we need next,\u201d so the question becomes investigable instead of opinionated.","Good problem questions preserve uncertainty and make it actionable.","If you don\u2019t force \u201cclarifying questions,\u201d the model will fake certainty by inventing causes. That feels helpful\u2014and it\u2019s exactly how teams chase the wrong thing.",B.aiZ,B.M6)
B.a1p=new A.b("Require a single diagnostic question (not generic advice)",!0)
B.a2i=new A.b("Force definitions for \u201cslow\u201d (mark as [Unknown] if missing)",!0)
B.a2U=new A.b("Force when/where it occurs (mark as [Unknown] if missing)",!0)
B.a1r=new A.b("Ban solutions in the output",!0)
B.a2o=new A.b("Require 3 specific data points to collect next",!0)
B.Su=new A.b("Ask for a list of optimisation tips",!1)
B.Ys=new A.b("Assume the backend is the problem",!1)
B.a20=new A.b("Write a long explanation of why systems slow down",!1)
B.a6v=new A.b("Remove unknowns to make it sound confident",!1)
B.a6a=new A.b("Add emotional urgency to motivate action",!1)
B.NW=s([B.a1p,B.a2i,B.a2U,B.a1r,B.a2o,B.Su,B.Ys,B.a20,B.a6v,B.a6a],t.W)
B.aiQ=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that turn a vague complaint into an evidence-driven diagnostic question.",B.NW,"Your edge is precision: definitions + evidence. This stops the model from turning complaints into generic \u201cbest practices.\u201d","Rewrite into one actionable diagnostic question. Define what \u201cslow\u201d means and when/where it occurs (mark unknowns). No solutions. Output one question + 3 data points to collect next.","You\u2019re now converting complaints into investigations\u2014most people skip definitions and get useless optimisation advice.","Rewrite the complaint into one actionable diagnostic question. Define what \u201cslow\u201d refers to and when/where it happens (mark unknowns). Do not propose solutions. Output: one question plus three data points to collect next.")
B.aa3=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *operational definition*.\n- Requirements forced definitions for \u201cslow\u201d and when/where it occurs\n- Expectations required data collection, not solutions\n- Objective produced a question that multiple teams can align on (same evidence, same target)")
B.a9m=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nRewrite this complaint into a question\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite into one actionable diagnostic question. Define what \u201cslow\u201d means and when/where it happens (mark unknowns). Do not propose solutions. Output one question + 3 data points to collect next.")
B.a8r=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nVague complaint with multiple plausible meanings\n\nO - Objective\nTranslate into a diagnostic question teams can act on\n\nR - Requirements\nDefine \u201cslow\u201d; specify where/when; no solutions; mark unknowns\n\nE - Expectations\nOne diagnostic question + 3 data points to collect")
B.MJ=s([B.aa3,B.a9m,B.a8r],t.c)
B.adM=new A.ab("Turn complaints into actionable questions","You receive vague complaints like \u201cthe system is slow.\u201d\n\nThe complaint could mean latency, timeouts, poor UX, or an upstream dependency\u2014and different teams will interpret it differently.\n\nIf you ask AI a generic question, you\u2019ll get generic optimisation advice.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - vague complaint with multiple plausible meanings\n- Objective - translate it into an actionable diagnostic question\n- Requirements - specify where/when it happens, what \u201cslow\u201d means, and what signal would confirm a cause\n- Expectations - one diagnostic question + what data to collect","Rewrite the complaint into a single, actionable diagnostic question.\n\nRequirements:\n- Define what \u201cslow\u201d refers to (response time, timeouts, perceived lag) as [Unknown] if not stated\n- Specify when/where it happens (e.g., peak hours, specific workflow) as [Unknown] if not stated\n- Do not propose solutions\n- Output format:\n  1) One diagnostic question\n  2) 3 data points to collect next\n\nReturn only the output.","**Diagnostic question**\nWhat is driving slow system responsiveness during peak usage, and is the delay caused by backend processing time, network latency, or client-side rendering?\n\n**Data to collect (next)**\n- Response-time breakdown by stage (client -> network -> server -> database) [Unknown]\n- Error/timeout rates and correlation with peak periods [Unknown]\n- Workflow/endpoint-specific latency hotspots (top 5) [Unknown]\n\nLook at how the question becomes actionable: the prompt forces definitions and evidence needs instead of letting \u201cslow\u201d remain a vibe.","Define the problem in evidence terms before you ask for fixes.","\u201cActionable\u201d means you can collect evidence. If you don\u2019t force data points, the model will jump to solutions and you\u2019ll waste a week \u201coptimising\u201d the wrong layer.",B.aiQ,B.MJ)
B.a_N=new A.b("Ban cause assumptions (don\u2019t guess)",!0)
B.UQ=new A.b("Clarify what \u201cwrong\u201d means (generation vs correctness) and mark unknowns",!0)
B.a4T=new A.b("Require one precise investigative question (failure-mode focused)",!0)
B.Y0=new A.b("Require a 4-step triage checklist (what to check first)",!0)
B.a0g=new A.b("Return only the output in the specified format",!0)
B.VS=new A.b("Ask for likely root causes",!1)
B.a_H=new A.b("Write a detailed explanation of reporting systems",!1)
B.a1U=new A.b("Assume it\u2019s a permissions issue",!1)
B.W1=new A.b("Remove unknowns to make it confident",!1)
B.a0j=new A.b("Give recommendations to fix it immediately",!1)
B.Iq=s([B.a_N,B.UQ,B.a4T,B.Y0,B.a0g,B.VS,B.a_H,B.a1U,B.W1,B.a0j],t.W)
B.ahY=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that turn an ambiguous request into a precise investigative question with triage.",B.Iq,"The expert move is splitting failure modes and forcing triage. This prevents confident guessing and gets you to evidence faster.","Rewrite into one precise investigative question. Don\u2019t assume cause. Clarify what \u201creports\u201d refers to; mark unknowns. Output one question + a 4-step triage checklist. Return only the output.","You now control ambiguity without guessing\u2014this is how you move faster than \u201csmart-sounding\u201d analysis.","Rewrite the request into one precise investigative question. Do not assume the cause. Clarify what \u201creports\u201d refers to (generation failure vs incorrect numbers) and mark unknowns as [Unknown]. Output: one question plus a 4-step triage checklist. Return only the output.")
B.a85=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *failure-mode precision*.\n- Requirements banned cause assumptions and forced missing fields to be marked\n- Expectations produced a triage checklist, not a vague question\n- Objective turned \u201ccheck reports\u201d into an investigation you can execute immediately")
B.aag=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nRewrite this as a better question\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite into one precise investigative question. Don\u2019t assume cause. Clarify what \u201creports\u201d refers to (mark [Unknown] if missing). Output one question + a 4-step triage checklist.")
B.a95=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nAmbiguous request with multiple failure modes\n\nO - Objective\nA precise question that drives first-pass investigation\n\nR - Requirements\nNo cause assumptions; clarify \u201cwrong\u201d; mark unknowns\n\nE - Expectations\nOne question + 4-step triage checklist")
B.MN=s([B.a85,B.aag,B.a95],t.c)
B.adw=new A.ab("Turn ambiguous requests into precise questions","Someone asks, \u201cCan you check what\u2019s happening with the reports?\u201d\n\nThat could mean missing data, a pipeline failure, a permissions issue, or \u201cthe numbers look weird.\u201d\n\nIf you turn this into a shallow question, you\u2019ll get a shallow answer\u2014and then you still won\u2019t know what to check.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - ambiguous request with multiple failure modes\n- Objective - turn it into a precise investigative question\n- Requirements - specify what \u201cwrong\u201d means, what to verify first, and what evidence is needed\n- Expectations - one question + a triage checklist","Rewrite the request into a precise investigative question.\n\nRequirements:\n- Do not assume the cause\n- Clarify what \u201creports\u201d refers to (generation failure vs incorrect numbers) as [Unknown] if not stated\n- Output format:\n  1) One precise question\n  2) A 4-step triage checklist (what to check first)\n\nReturn only the output.","**Precise question**\nWhat exactly is failing with the reports (generation, delivery, or correctness of numbers), and which part of the reporting pipeline should we verify first to isolate the failure mode?\n\n**Triage checklist (first pass)**\n1) Confirm the failure mode: not generated vs generated-but-wrong vs delayed [Unknown]\n2) Identify scope: which reports, which time range, which users [Unknown]\n3) Check recent changes: deployments/config/data source changes [Unknown]\n4) Verify pipeline checkpoints: ingestion -> transformation -> aggregation -> dashboard [Unknown]\n\nThe difference is triage control: the prompt forces a failure-mode question and a first-pass checklist, so you can act even before you have perfect information.","Precision is the ability to investigate without guessing.","Most people try to \u201csound smart\u201d by guessing the cause. Don\u2019t. Force a failure-mode split and triage steps\u2014this is how you look competent without pretending you know.",B.ahY,B.MN)
B.Ja=s([B.aeG,B.adM,B.adw],t.r)
B.Ha=new A.bR("Turn Problems Into Clear AI Questions",B.Ja,null)
