B.ahE=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that keep SWOT evidence-based.",B.Ls,"Strategy frameworks need the same honesty as analytics prompts: tag unknowns or you get confident fiction.","SWOT: sales meeting AI; <=3/quadrant; evidence tags; [Unknown]; blind spots.","You made SWOT operational\u2014evidence tags turn meetings into decisions.","Create a SWOT for an AI meeting-notes assistant aimed at sales teams. Use at most three bullets per quadrant. Each bullet must label its support as (Data), (Customer), (Competitor), or [Unknown] when evidence is missing. Competitors may be partially unknown\u2014mark gaps explicitly. Finish with a short \u201cBlind spots\u201d list of evidence you still need to collect.")
B.a9M=new A.k("What Made This Work","SWOT stopped being vibes because bullets carried evidence types.\n- Context scoped product + audience\n- Objective aimed at challengeable output\n- Requirements capped count and tagged proof or [Unknown]\n- Expectations surfaced blind spots explicitly")
B.a8c=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nSWOT for our product\n\nStrong prompt:\nSales meeting AI; <=3 bullets/quadrant; evidence tags; [Unknown]; blind spots list.")
B.a9I=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nAI notes for sales; partial competitor info\n\nO - Objective\nActionable SWOT leadership can test\n\nR - Requirements\nEvidence tags; caps; honest unknowns\n\nE - Expectations\nBlind spots section")
B.Kg=s([B.a9M,B.a8c,B.a9I],t.c)
B.aea=new A.ab("SWOT with evidence discipline","SWOT collapses into opinions unless you force evidence rules.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - product, segment, and competitive set (named or [Unknown])\n- Objective - produce a SWOT that leadership can challenge constructively\n- Requirements - each bullet must cite evidence type (customer quote, metric, competitor move) or [Unknown]\n- Expectations - max 3 bullets per quadrant","Build a SWOT for our AI meeting-notes assistant aimed at sales teams.\n\nCompetitors: [Unknown full list].\n\nRequirements: max 3 bullets per quadrant; each bullet tags evidence as (Data), (Customer), (Competitor), or [Unknown].\n\nExpectations: include a \u201cBlind spots\u201d line listing what evidence we still need.","**Strengths**\n- Fast time-to-value for reps who hate CRM hygiene (Customer) [Unknown sample size]\n- Differentiated live-capture mode vs static summaries (Data) [Unknown benchmark]\n\n**Weaknesses**\n- Privacy review slows enterprise rollout (Customer)\n- Accuracy drops on noisy calls (Data) [Unknown rate]\n\n**Opportunities**\n- CRMs pushing deeper call intelligence (Competitor) [Unknown]\n- Managers want coaching insights, not transcripts (Customer)\n\n**Threats**\n- Incumbents bundle similar features (Competitor) [Unknown]\n\n**Blind spots**\nWin/loss data on pricing, legal blockers in regulated industries [Unknown]\n\nFrameworks work when Requirements turn quadrants into evidence lists.","Frameworks are fancy tables until Requirements demand proof types.","If every SWOT bullet starts with \u201cwe believe,\u201d you skipped Requirements for evidence.",B.ahE,B.Kg)
B.a5p=new A.b("State initiative scope and time horizon in Context",!0)
B.a4J=new A.b("Objective: expose assumptions that could invalidate the plan",!0)
