B.Lo=s([B.U8,B.Ti,B.a27,B.Sv,B.a62,B.SU,B.a6o,B.YA,B.a3l,B.Sx],t.W)
B.ahL=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that keep a one-chart slide honest and decision-ready.",B.Lo,"Slide credibility is built by boundaries: what the chart shows, what it doesn\u2019t, and what decision it supports.","Propose one exec-chart: chart type + axes, caption, and a \u201cLimits\u201d bullet. No invented numbers or causal claims.","You now control chart honesty - most decks skip limits and accidentally mislead.","Recommend ONE chart for an exec slide: type, axes, one-sentence caption, and one \u201cLimits\u201d bullet. Tie to decision signal. No invented numbers or causality.")
B.abS=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is honest framing: chart spec + caption + limits. Without limits, AI will add causal language by default.\n- Requirements ban invented numbers and force a \u201cLimits\u201d guardrail\n- Objective selects decision-driving signal, not the prettiest metric\n- Expectations produce slide-ready output quickly")
B.ab0=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nPick the best chart for this deck\n\nStrong prompt:\nGiven these metrics, propose ONE chart for an executive deck. Output: chart type, x/y axes, one-sentence chart caption, and one \u201cLimits\u201d bullet stating what the chart does NOT prove. Do not invent numbers or interpretation.")
B.a9q=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nMultiple metrics, single-chart constraint\n\nO - Objective\nSelect decision-driving chart and honest framing\n\nR - Requirements\nChart spec; caption; \u201cLimits\u201d bullet; no invented numbers/interpretation\n\nE - Expectations\nSlide-ready chart recommendation")
B.LW=s([B.abS,B.ab0,B.a9q],t.c)
B.aey=new A.ab("Extract the \u201cOne Chart That Matters\u201d Without Misleading","You have multiple metrics, but the deck can only include one chart.\n\nThe risk is cherry-picking or hiding counter-signal that leadership cares about.\n\nIf you choose the wrong chart framing, you\u2019ll drive the wrong decision.\n\nIf you prompt AI weakly, it usually:\n- picks the most impressive metric\n- ignores counter-metrics\n- adds interpretation that isn\u2019t supported\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- no rule for selecting the decision-driving metric\n- no requirement to state what the chart does not prove\n- no expectation for an honest caption\n\nMost people optimize for \u201clooks good.\u201d\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - multiple metrics, single-chart constraint\n- Objective - pick the decision-driving chart and honest framing\n- Requirements - chart type, caption, limits of inference\n- Expectations - a slide-ready chart spec + caption","Given these metrics, propose ONE chart for an executive deck. Output: chart type, x/y axes, one-sentence chart caption, and one \u201cLimits\u201d bullet stating what the chart does NOT prove. Do not invent numbers or interpretation.","**Recommended chart**: Line chart (trend over time)\n- X-axis: Weeks (last 8\u201312)\n- Y-axis: Completion rate (or primary success metric)\n\n**Caption**: \u201cPrimary success metric trend over time to assess whether rollout is stabilizing.\u201d\n\n**Limits**: This chart does not prove causality or isolate which workstream caused the change.\n\nThis is where you can see control: the prompt forced a \u201cLimits\u201d line, which prevents the model from turning the chart into a story it can\u2019t support.","Every chart needs a caption and a limit.","If you don\u2019t require a \u201cLimits\u201d line, you\u2019re asking the model to do persuasion. In executive decks, persuasion without boundaries becomes misinformation.",B.ahL,B.LW)
B.a6T=new A.b("Require In Scope / Out of Scope / Conditions to Revisit sections",!0)
B.XR=new A.b("Fix bullet counts so it stays crisp",!0)
B.a_s=new A.b("Require neutral tone and ban blame language",!0)
