B.aiz=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that extract decisions and action items without invented completeness.",B.Mk,"Most summaries break trust by hiding gaps. \u201cOpen Questions + [Unknown]\u201d is how you keep alignment without guessing.","Summarise into Decisions, Action Items, Open Questions. Facts only; no invented owners/dates. Mark missing details [Unknown]. Keep concise and forward-safe. Return only the summary.","You\u2019re now extracting decisions without inventing certainty\u2014this is where you gain an operational advantage.","Summarise the email into three sections: Decisions, Action Items, Open Questions. Use confirmed facts only. Do not invent owners or dates; mark missing details as [Unknown]. Keep concise and forward-safe. Return only the summary.")
B.acH=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *decision extraction with bounded certainty*.\n- Expectations forced a decision format (Decisions / Actions / Questions)\n- Requirements banned invented owners/dates and used [Unknown]\n- Objective prevented a \u201cnice recap\u201d that still leaves the team misaligned")
B.a8P=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nSummarise this email\n\nStrong prompt:\nSummarise into Decisions, Action Items, Open Questions. Facts only; no invented owners/dates. Mark missing details [Unknown]. Keep concise and forward-safe. Return only the summary.")
B.abW=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nNoisy email thread with implied commitments\n\nO - Objective\nAlign on decisions, actions, and open questions\n\nR - Requirements\nFacts only; no invention; [Unknown] for missing owners/dates\n\nE - Expectations\n3 sections: Decisions / Action Items / Open Questions")
B.Jn=s([B.acH,B.a8P,B.abW],t.c)
B.aeA=new A.ab("Summarise an Email Into Key Points","You have a long email thread with scattered decisions and implied commitments.\n\nPeople are already acting on different interpretations.\n\nIf your summary misses one decision, the team will execute the wrong plan.\n\nWeak prompting usually produces:\n- a generic recap with no decisions\n- invented \u201cnext steps\u201d to look helpful\n- softened language that hides risk\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - decision extraction from noisy email\n- Objective - align everyone on decisions, owners, and open questions\n- Requirements - facts only; separate decisions vs open questions; no invention\n- Expectations - structured bullets that are easy to forward","Summarise the email into key points.\n\nRequirements:\n- Output 3 sections with bullets: Decisions, Action Items, Open Questions\n- Use only confirmed information; do not invent owners/dates\n- If an owner/date is missing, mark it [Unknown]\n- Keep it concise and forward-safe\n\nReturn only the summary.","**Decisions**\n- Meeting moved to Thursday\n\n**Action Items**\n- Share the updated agenda once ready [Owner: Unknown]\n\n**Open Questions**\n- When will the agenda be ready? [Unknown]\n\nNotice how uncertainty is handled explicitly: [Unknown] keeps the summary credible instead of \u201ccomplete-looking.\u201d","A useful summary preserves uncertainty instead of hiding it.","Summaries fail when they look \u201ccomplete\u201d but aren\u2019t. Force Open Questions and [Unknown] so missing information stays visible instead of silently guessed.",B.aiz,B.Jn)
B.a3O=new A.b("Separate Agreed Actions vs Proposed Ideas vs Open Decisions",!0)
B.a_X=new A.b("Require Owner and Due Date fields for each action",!0)
B.a_g=new A.b("Mark missing Owner/Due Date as [Unknown]",!0)
B.a6d=new A.b("Ban invented decisions, owners, or deadlines",!0)
B.a5U=new A.b("Keep tone neutral and operational",!0)
B.WL=new A.b("Resolve open decisions to sound decisive",!1)
B.Wh=new A.b("Invent owners based on seniority",!1)
B.UU=new A.b("Add deadlines to create urgency",!1)
B.X6=new A.b("Write a long narrative summary paragraph",!1)
B.a3K=new A.b("Remove \u201cproposed ideas\u201d to reduce confusion",!1)
B.NU=s([B.a3O,B.a_X,B.a_g,B.a6d,B.a5U,B.WL,B.Wh,B.UU,B.X6,B.a3K],t.W)
B.ahB=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that turn messy notes into action steps without inventing alignment.",B.NU,"The highest-risk failure is \u201ccleaning\u201d ambiguity into fake certainty. Preserve the buckets so execution matches reality.","Summarise notes into Agreed Actions, Proposed Ideas (not decided), Open Decisions. Include Owner and Due Date for actions; mark missing as [Unknown]. Don\u2019t invent decisions/owners/deadlines. Return only the summary.","You\u2019re now producing meeting outputs that drive action without creating fake commitments.","Summarise meeting notes into three sections: Agreed Actions, Proposed Ideas (not decided), Open Decisions. For actions include Owner and Due Date; mark missing as [Unknown]. Do not invent decisions, owners, or deadlines. Neutral, operational tone.")
B.a8q=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *certainty hygiene*.\n- Expectations forced three certainty buckets (Agreed / Proposed / Open)\n- Requirements prevented invented owners/dates and used [Unknown]\n- Objective produced actionability without fake alignment")
B.a8I=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nTurn these notes into action items\n\nStrong prompt:\nSummarise into Agreed Actions, Proposed Ideas (not decided), Open Decisions. For each action include Owner/Due Date; mark missing as [Unknown]. Do not invent decisions/owners/deadlines. Return only the summary.")
B.a9c=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nMessy meeting notes with mixed certainty\n\nO - Objective\nActionability without pretending decisions are final\n\nR - Requirements\nSeparate certainty buckets; no invention; [Unknown] for missing owner/date\n\nE - Expectations\n3 sections with structured action items")
B.Jw=s([B.a8q,B.a8I,B.a9c],t.c)
B.aen=new A.ab("Summarise Meeting Notes into Actionable Steps","Your meeting notes are messy: partial decisions, half-formed ideas, and unresolved debates.\n\nIf you summarise as if things are decided, you create fake alignment.\n\nIf you summarise as raw notes, nobody acts.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - messy notes with mixed certainty\n- Objective - action plan + open decisions\n- Requirements - separate decided vs proposed vs unknown; no invention\n- Expectations - clear action list with owners/dates marked if missing","Summarise the meeting notes into actionable steps.\n\nRequirements:\n- Output 3 sections: Agreed Actions, Proposed Ideas (not decided), Open Decisions\n- For each action, include Owner and Due Date; if missing, mark [Owner: Unknown] / [Due: Unknown]\n- Do not invent decisions, owners, or deadlines\n- Keep tone neutral and operational\n\nReturn only the summary.","**Agreed Actions**\n- Share the updated agenda [Owner: Unknown] [Due: Unknown]\n\n**Proposed Ideas (not decided)**\n- Review the draft before revisions are finalised [Unknown]\n\n**Open Decisions**\n- Confirm revision scope before finalising [Unknown]\n\nThe control point is certainty hygiene: the prompt forced separation of decided vs proposed so the output doesn\u2019t pretend the meeting was cleaner than it was.","Meeting summaries should preserve what\u2019s unresolved.","If you don\u2019t explicitly separate \u201cproposed\u201d from \u201cagreed,\u201d the model will \u201cclean up\u201d by turning suggestions into commitments. That\u2019s how teams ship the wrong work.",B.ahB,B.Jw)
B.yG=new A.b("Exactly one sentence",!0)
B.a0T=new A.b("Preserve original intent",!0)
B.Zz=new A.b("Facts only (no invented specifics)",!0)
B.W8=new A.b("Plain, quoteable tone (no hype)",!0)
B.XG=new A.b("Return only the sentence (no extras)",!0)
B.SR=new A.b("Add a confident claim to make it strong",!1)
B.a6D=new A.b("Use persuasive language to increase impact",!1)
B.Ws=new A.b("Include multiple sentences for nuance",!1)
B.a60=new A.b("Add likely details to sound complete",!1)
