B.aiV=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that make this a strong prompt for a colleague email\u2014report ready for review and comments by Wednesday.",B.O0,"A premium prompt names Context, Objective, Requirements, and Expectations\u2014what the output should include\u2014so the model can deliver something you can send.","Write a professional email to a colleague explaining that the report is ready for review. The objective is to clearly request comments by Wednesday. Write the email in two short paragraphs using a polite and professional tone. The final output should be clear, concise, and ready to send.","That score is the gap between \u201csounds fine\u201d and send-ready: miss one C.O.R.E. slot and the model fills it with guesswork.",null)
B.aaj=new A.k("What Made This Work","This is what changes the output: the model is following your structure, not polishing your writing.\n- Context pins who this is for\n- Objective pins the deadline ask\n- Requirements cap length and tone\n- Expectations demand send-ready text")
B.ac3=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nWrite an email about a document\n\nStrong prompt:\nWrite a professional email explaining that the draft policy document is ready for review and asking if they can share feedback by Thursday. Keep it to two or three short paragraphs.")
B.acX=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nColleague email; draft policy document is ready for review\n\nO - Objective\nRequest feedback by Thursday\n\nR - Requirements\nProfessional tone; two to three short paragraphs\n\nE - Expectations\nThe email should be clear and ready to send")
B.O5=s([B.aaj,B.ac3,B.acX],t.c)
B.aep=new A.ab("Write a Professional Email","You need to write a professional email to a colleague.\n\nThe draft policy document is ready, and you want to ask for feedback by Thursday.\n\nBut when you give AI a vague instruction, the result is usually:\n- too generic\n- missing the actual request\n- not ready to send\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- no clear Objective\n- weak Requirements\n- no defined Expectations\n\nMost people would type \u201cwrite an email about the policy\u201d\u2014then wonder why the reply feels generic.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - what is happening\n- Objective - what the email should achieve\n- Requirements - tone and structure\n- Expectations - what the final output should include","Write a professional email explaining that the draft policy document is ready for review and asking if they can share feedback by Thursday. Keep it to two or three short paragraphs.","Subject: Draft Policy Document Ready for Review\n\nHi [Name],\n\nI'm writing to let you know that the draft policy document is now ready for review. Please feel free to take a look at your convenience.\n\nIf possible, could you share your feedback by Thursday? This will help us stay on track with the timeline. Let me know if you have any questions.\n\nThanks,\n[Your Name]\n\nNotice how the deadline and the ask stay explicit\u2014that is your Objective and Expectations, not the model improvising \u201cprofessional.\u201d","AI mirrors the frame you give it. Name the situation, the outcome, the format, and what \u201cdone\u201d looks like\u2014and you pull ahead of anyone still typing \u201cmake this sound good.\u201d","People skip C.O.R.E. because one line feels faster\u2014then they lose the evening fixing mush. The real mistake is treating structure as optional.",B.aiV,B.O5)
