B.ahX=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that make this a strong prompt for turning a casual client chat into a polite email that confirms a Tuesday wire transfer without adding new promises.",B.M1,"When tone is the job, C.O.R.E. still matters: audience, outcome, tone and length rules, and a defined send-ready artifact.","Turn this casual client chat into a short polite email confirming the wire transfer is scheduled for Tuesday. Name the audience and email format, keep a courteous professional tone in two or three sentences, do not invent amounts or bank details, and deliver text ready to send.","Full marks is the advantage: most people lose here because \u201ctone\u201d without fact-lock drifts\u2014your picks keep meaning and register under control.","Draft a brief client email confirming the wire transfer is on track for Tuesday. Keep a courteous professional tone in two or three sentences, do not invent amounts or banking details, and leave the message ready to send.")
B.a9Y=new A.k("What Made This Work","This is what changes the output: tone prompts fail when \u201cprofessional\u201d is the only instruction\u2014the model will rewrite meaning.\n- Context names leadership email so register shifts correctly\n- Objective keeps timing + no-reply as the only job\n- Requirements lock facts and sentence count\n- Expectations demand send-ready lines, not a new pitch")
B.ab3=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nMake this sound professional\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite this line for a leadership email without changing facts: I'll drop the revised budget memo later today\u2014no need to reply yet. Keep the meaning identical, use a professional tone, and limit the output to two short sentences.")
B.a88=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nLeadership email; budget memo revision timing\n\nO - Objective\nShare timing; state no reply needed\n\nR - Requirements\nProfessional tone; same facts; two short sentences\n\nE - Expectations\nPolished lines ready to send")
B.K7=s([B.a9Y,B.ab3,B.a88],t.c)
B.aeD=new A.ab("Polish a Casual Update for a Formal Audience",'You wrote a quick Slack-style line for a leadership email: you will share the revised budget memo later today and people do not need to reply yet.\n\nThe audience expects a calm, professional register\u2014not chatty shorthand.\n\nWhen you only say "make this professional," AI often:\n- adds filler\n- shifts the meaning\n- sounds stiff or generic\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- no clear Objective\n- weak Requirements\n- no defined Expectations\n\nMost users say \u201cmake it professional\u201d and get a new promise or a new tone\u2014because they never locked the facts.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - leadership email; memo still being revised\n- Objective - communicate timing and no action required\n- Requirements - professional tone; keep the same facts; two short sentences\n- Expectations - ready to send; no new commitments',"Rewrite this line for a leadership email without changing facts: I'll drop the revised budget memo later today\u2014no need to reply yet. Keep the meaning identical, use a professional tone, and limit the output to two short sentences.","Subject: Revised budget memo\n\nDear [Name],\n\nI will share the revised budget memo later today. No response is required at this stage.\n\nKind regards,\n[Your Name]\n\nNotice how meaning stayed frozen\u2014Requirements + Expectations told the model what not to change, not just how to sound.","Tone is a constraint problem: lock audience, facts, and length first\u2014style follows, and you stay ahead of generic \u201crewrite\u201d output.","If you do not say \u201csame facts,\u201d the model will \u201cimprove\u201d you into commitments you did not make\u2014then you are editing on defense.",B.ahX,B.K7)
B.WO=new A.b("The prompt should state that the input bullets conflict and must be reconciled",!0)
B.a56=new A.b("The objective should be to inform internal stakeholders of the new launch window",!0)
B.a4w=new A.b("The requirements should enforce neutral executive tone and a fixed length",!0)
B.a23=new A.b("The prompt should forbid inventing causes, owners, or dates not in the notes",!0)
B.a3B=new A.b("The expectation should be a memo ready to circulate without edits",!0)
