B.Zw=new A.b("Request a ten-page appendix",!1)
B.a5K=new A.b("Tell the model to compare LLM providers",!1)
B.LN=s([B.a3Z,B.a_o,B.VH,B.WW,B.XK,B.a6V,B.a2Y,B.UR,B.Zw,B.a5K],t.W)
B.air=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that make this a strong prompt for asking a vendor for a one-week extension on a contract review while keeping the partnership positive.",B.LN,"Boundary-setting emails need context, a crisp ask, tone rules, and a no-fabrication line\u2014otherwise the model swings between groveling and blunt refusals.","Email the vendor asking for a one-week extension on the contract review, propose a new return date, cite one factual scheduling constraint without drama, keep the tone collaborative, and keep the message under a hundred words.","That is high-signal: boundary prompts fail when Objective is mush\u2014your answers show you can trade time without trading away credibility.","Write a concise vendor email requesting one more week for the contract review, propose a specific new date, reference one factual scheduling constraint without blame, stay collaborative, and keep it ready to send at under a hundred words.")
B.abk=new A.k("What Made This Work","This is what changes the output: boundary emails need competing objectives named up front\u2014otherwise the model picks apology or aggression.\n- Objective pairs decline with an alternate path\n- Requirements cap promises so you cannot \u201chelpfully\u201d lie\n- Expectations force send-ready structure with a next step")
B.aau=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nSay no politely\n\nStrong prompt:\nWrite a short email to a stakeholder who asked for a full analysis by 9 a.m. tomorrow. Explain that a reviewable draft needs until Thursday morning, offer a concise interim summary tomorrow if helpful, and keep the tone respectful and confident. Do not promise legal sign-off or resources you cannot guarantee. Limit to about ninety words.")
B.aax=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nStakeholder email; unrealistic morning deadline\n\nO - Objective\nDecline unsafe timing; propose viable date; preserve trust\n\nR - Requirements\nRespectful confident tone; word cap; no false promises\n\nE - Expectations\nSend-ready email with clear next step")
B.MO=s([B.abk,B.aau,B.aax],t.c)
B.aeF=new A.ab("Hold a Boundary on Timing Without Sounding Dismissive",'A stakeholder asks for your team\'s deep-dive analysis "by 9 a.m. tomorrow"\u2014but your team needs at least until Thursday for anything reviewable.\n\nYou must decline the 9 a.m. deadline without damaging the relationship.\n\nA vague prompt produces:\n- over-apologising\n- fake certainty\n- or an aggressive "no"\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- unclear Objective\n- weak Requirements\n- no defined Expectations\n\nMost people ask AI to \u201csay no nicely\u201d and get either groveling or a fight-pick\u2014because boundaries were never defined.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - stakeholder request; unrealistic 9 a.m. deadline\n- Objective - decline 9 a.m. push; propose Thursday deliverable; keep trust\n- Requirements - respectful, confident tone; short; no invented approvals\n- Expectations - email ready to send',"Write a short email to a stakeholder who asked for a full analysis by 9 a.m. tomorrow. Explain that a reviewable draft needs until Thursday morning, offer a concise interim summary tomorrow if helpful, and keep the tone respectful and confident. Do not promise legal sign-off or resources you cannot guarantee. Limit to about ninety words.","Subject: Timing for the analysis\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThanks for the request. A reviewable version of the full analysis needs until Thursday morning to meet our quality bar.\n\nIf helpful, I can share a brief interim summary tomorrow so you have directional visibility sooner. Let me know what level of detail would be most useful.\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\n\nNotice how the no is paired with a smaller yes\u2014the Objective trades timing without inventing leverage you do not have.","Timing conflicts are negotiation prompts: say what ships, what does not, and what is off-limits\u2014most users only ask for politeness.","If you do not forbid false promises, the model will \u201cclose\u201d the deal for you\u2014then you own commitments you never approved.",B.air,B.MO)
B.IW=s([B.aeD,B.adO,B.aeF],t.r)
B.Hk=new A.bR("Adjust Tone for Any Situation",B.IW,null)
