B.aij=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that produce an exec-ready Outcome/Risk/Ask without invented certainty.",B.Oa,"This is where most AI users fail: they ask for \u201cexec tone\u201d and get confident vagueness. Force structure + bounded certainty so the output stays decision-ready.","Rewrite for senior leadership as exactly 3 bullets: Outcome, Risk, Ask. Facts only. Mark gaps [Unknown]. No invented mitigations. Return only the bullets.","You\u2019re now writing exec updates that trigger decisions instead of consuming attention.","Rewrite for senior leadership using exactly 3 bullets: Outcome, Risk, Ask. Facts only; mark unknowns as [Unknown]. Keep concise and forward-safe. Do not invent mitigations. Return only the bullets.")
B.aah=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *decision structure under uncertainty*.\n- Requirements forced bounded certainty ([Unknown] instead of confident guessing)\n- Expectations locked the exec lens (Outcome/Risk/Ask)\n- Objective ensured the update produces a decision, not information noise")
B.aaG=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nRewrite for senior leadership\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite for senior leadership. Output exactly 3 bullets: Outcome, Risk, Ask. Facts only; mark gaps [Unknown]. Keep concise and forward-safe. Do not invent mitigation claims. Return only the bullets.")
B.aaW=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nExec audience, skim speed, forward-safe\n\nO - Objective\nOutcomes + risk + decision ask\n\nR - Requirements\nFacts only; [Unknown] for gaps; no invented mitigations; concise\n\nE - Expectations\nExactly 3 bullets: Outcome, Risk, Ask")
B.L6=s([B.aah,B.aaG,B.aaW],t.c)
B.adt=new A.ab("Rewrite for a Senior Leadership Audience","You\u2019re turning an internal update into something senior leadership can read in 20 seconds.\n\nThey don\u2019t want process\u2014they want outcomes, risk, and the decision ask.\n\nIf you oversimplify, you hide the only thing that matters.\n\nIf you prompt AI weakly, it usually:\n- strips risk to sound \u201cconfident\u201d\n- adds vague positivity\n- removes the decision ask entirely\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - exec skim update\n- Objective - outcomes + risk + ask, no fluff\n- Requirements - high-level, bounded certainty, no invention\n- Expectations - short, forward-safe format","Rewrite the update for senior leadership.\n\nRequirements:\n- Output exactly 3 bullets: Outcome, Risk, Ask\n- Use only confirmed facts; if a detail is missing, mark it [Unknown]\n- Keep it concise and forward-safe\n- Do not add mitigation claims unless stated\n\nReturn only the 3 bullets.","- **Outcome:** The project remains on track for Friday\u2019s milestone based on confirmed progress to date.\n- **Risk:** Final validation is in progress; residual risk cannot be quantified yet [Unknown].\n- **Ask:** Confirm whether to proceed with the milestone pending validation, or hold until results are confirmed.\n\nThis is where you can see executive control: the prompt forced Outcome/Risk/Ask so leadership gets a decision signal, not \u201can update.\u201d","For senior audiences, structure is how you earn attention.","Executives don\u2019t need more detail\u2014they need the *decision boundary*. If you don\u2019t force an Ask, the model will write \u201cnext steps\u201d that don\u2019t drive action.",B.aij,B.L6)
