B.aj2=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that make a customer update calm and clear without accidental promises.",B.M0,"The trap is \u201chelpful certainty.\u201d You want reassurance *inside boundaries*, not invented commitments that become someone else\u2019s contract.","Rewrite for a customer: calm and respectful. Facts only; no invented timelines/causes/guarantees. Include what we know, what we\u2019re doing next, and when we\u2019ll update. If unknown, say it\u2019s being investigated.","You now control customer tone without over-committing\u2014most users accidentally prompt the model into making promises.","Rewrite for a customer in a calm, confident, respectful tone. Use confirmed facts only. Do not invent timelines, causes, or guarantees. Include what we know, what we\u2019ll do next, and when we\u2019ll update. If something is unknown, say it\u2019s being investigated.")
B.a8V=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *reassurance without guarantees*.\n- Requirements prevented invented timelines/causes\n- Expectations forced a complete customer structure (know / next / update)\n- Objective kept the message calm and credible instead of vague or risky")
B.a9C=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nRewrite this for a customer\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite for a customer: calm, confident, respectful. Facts only; no invented timelines/causes/guarantees. Include what we know, what we\u2019re doing next, and when we\u2019ll update. If unknown, say it\u2019s being investigated. Return only the rewrite.")
B.a8h=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nCustomer update with uncertainty and risk of over-commitment\n\nO - Objective\nClear, reassuring, credible communication\n\nR - Requirements\nFacts only; no guessing; tone constraints; investigation language for unknowns\n\nE - Expectations\nMessage includes: what we know / next / when we\u2019ll update")
B.NC=s([B.a8V,B.a9C,B.a8h],t.c)
B.adJ=new A.ab("Rewrite for a Customer Audience","You need to update a customer using text that currently reads like an internal note.\n\nYou must be clear, calm, and transparent\u2014without over-committing.\n\nIf you sound uncertain, you trigger escalations.\n\nIf you sound too certain, you create contractual expectations.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - customer-facing update\n- Objective - clarity + reassurance without false promises\n- Requirements - approved facts only; tone constraints; commitment boundaries\n- Expectations - short, customer-ready message","Rewrite the message for a customer.\n\nRequirements:\n- Keep tone calm, confident, and respectful\n- Use only confirmed facts; do not invent timelines, causes, or guarantees\n- Include: (1) what we know, (2) what we\u2019re doing next, (3) when we\u2019ll update them\n- If a detail is unknown, say it\u2019s being investigated (don\u2019t guess)\n\nReturn only the rewritten message.","Thank you for your patience. We\u2019re currently reviewing the issue and validating the impact based on the information available so far. Next, we\u2019ll complete our checks and share an update with the latest confirmed details by tomorrow.\n\nThe difference is controlled reassurance: the prompt forced a calm tone while banning invented certainty and over-promising.","Customer trust is built by credible certainty, not confident guessing.","Customers escalate when you guess. If you don\u2019t explicitly ban invented timelines, the model will \u201chelp\u201d by writing promises you can\u2019t keep.",B.aj2,B.NC)
B.TV=new A.b("Use plain language (avoid jargon)",!0)
B.So=new A.b("Keep key caveats/constraints visible",!0)
B.Yt=new A.b("Ban invented analogies and new examples",!0)
B.a5V=new A.b("Force structure: 2\u20133 sentences + one concrete example",!0)
B.SY=new A.b("Require the example to use only provided details",!0)
B.a4z=new A.b("Add jokes to keep it engaging",!1)
B.a1W=new A.b("Remove caveats to keep it simple",!1)
B.a0L=new A.b("Add new analogies to explain faster",!1)
B.a73=new A.b("Assume the audience is fully technical",!1)
B.a0P=new A.b("Expand into a long educational lesson",!1)
B.Kz=s([B.TV,B.So,B.Yt,B.a5V,B.SY,B.a4z,B.a1W,B.a0L,B.a73,B.a0P],t.W)
B.aib=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that make a non-expert rewrite clear, accurate, and respectful.",B.Kz,"The trap is \u201csimple but wrong.\u201d Protect constraints and ban invention so the non-expert version stays true and usable.","Rewrite for a non-expert: plain language, keep key caveats, no invented analogies. Output 2\u20133 sentences + one concrete example using only provided details. Return only the rewrite.","You\u2019re now simplifying without distortion\u2014most users trade accuracy for friendliness.","Rewrite for a non-expert audience using plain language. Keep key caveats/constraints. Do not invent analogies or new examples. Output: 2\u20133 sentences plus one concrete example using only provided details. Return only the rewritten content.")
B.abs=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *simplification without distortion*.\n- Requirements kept caveats visible (validation still pending)\n- Expectations demanded a specific shape (short explanation + example)\n- The \u201cno invented analogies\u201d rule prevents the model from changing meaning to be relatable")
B.acV=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nExplain this simply\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite for a non-expert audience: plain language, keep key caveats, no invented analogies. Output: 2\u20133 sentence explanation + one concrete example using only provided details. Return only the content.")
B.abJ=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nNon-expert audience, real constraints still matter\n\nO - Objective\nClarity without distortion or condescension\n\nR - Requirements\nPlain language; keep caveats; no invented analogies/examples\n\nE - Expectations\n2\u20133 sentence explanation + one concrete example (facts only)")
B.Iv=s([B.abs,B.acV,B.abJ],t.c)
B.adN=new A.ab("Rewrite for a Non-Expert Audience","You need to explain something to a non-expert audience without sounding condescending.\n\nIf it\u2019s too technical, they misunderstand.\n\nIf it\u2019s too simplified, you hide important constraints.\n\nWeak prompting often produces:\n- \u201cexplain like I\u2019m five\u201d tone that feels insulting\n- missing caveats that matter\n- invented analogies that change meaning\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - non-expert audience with real constraints\n- Objective - clarity without distortion\n- Requirements - plain language, keep key caveats, no invented analogies\n- Expectations - short explanation + one concrete example","Rewrite the text for a non-expert audience.\n\nRequirements:\n- Use plain language (avoid jargon)\n- Keep the key caveats/constraints (don\u2019t oversimplify)\n- Do not invent analogies or new examples\n- Include: (1) a 2\u20133 sentence explanation, (2) one concrete example using only provided details\n\nReturn only the rewritten content.","The project is on track, and we\u2019re in the final testing stage to make sure everything works as expected. We\u2019ll share the completed package once that validation is finished.\n\nExample: We\u2019re running the last checks now; when they pass, we\u2019ll send the final version.\n\nWhat matters here is respectful clarity: the prompt forced plain language while protecting the caveats that keep the explanation true.","Plain language is only valuable if the constraints survive.","Non-expert rewrites fail when the model tries to be \u201crelatable\u201d by inventing analogies. If you don\u2019t ban invention, you\u2019ll get clarity that\u2019s wrong.",B.aib,B.Iv)
B.N2=s([B.adt,B.adJ,B.adN],t.r)
B.Hn=new A.bR("Rewrite Content for Different Audiences",B.N2,u.k)
