B.ahV=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that make this a strong prompt for a two-sentence customer email about a service outage that emphasises restoration without overpromising future uptime.",B.Lx,"Sensitive plain-language updates need explicit tone, honesty limits, and a hard cap on promises.","Draft two customer-facing sentences confirming the outage is resolved, note active monitoring, do not guarantee uptime figures, stay calm, and avoid blame.","Sharp: this is where trust breaks\u2014your picks show you can cap promises and tone before the model writes a speech.","Write two calm customer sentences: service is restored, monitoring continues, no uptime guarantees, no blame, ready to send.")
B.a91=new A.k("What Made This Work","This is what changes the output: executive explanations fail when Objective is \u201csound smart.\u201d You need cause + mitigation + next checkpoint in plain English.\n- Requirements kill jargon and name-counting\n- Expectations force lines you can actually read aloud")
B.a9i=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nExplain the delay\n\nStrong prompt:\nWrite two sentences in plain language for executives explaining that the pilot slipped by two weeks because an upstream dependency delivered late, and that mitigation work is underway with a revised checkpoint next Friday. Keep the tone confident and calm, avoid jargon, and do not name individuals.")
B.a9w=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nExecutive update; pilot delay\n\nO - Objective\nExplain cause; show mitigation path\n\nR - Requirements\nPlain language; two sentences; calm tone; no names\n\nE - Expectations\nSpeaker-ready lines")
B.Lm=s([B.a91,B.a9i,B.a9w],t.c)
B.aeI=new A.ab("Explain a Setback in Plain Language for Executives","Leadership wants a short explanation of why a pilot slipped by two weeks. Engineering gave you dense jargon about dependencies.\n\nYou must sound honest and steady\u2014not defensive, not alarmist.\n\nWeak prompts produce:\n- buzzword soup\n- blame\n- or vague reassurance\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- unclear Objective\n- weak Requirements\n- no defined Expectations\n\nMost people \u201ctranslate jargon\u201d and smuggle blame in\u2014because plain language was never defined as a constraint.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - executive update; pilot slipped two weeks\n- Objective - explain cause at high level; show mitigation; no blame\n- Requirements - plain language; two sentences; confident calm tone\n- Expectations - ready for email or slide speaker notes","Write two sentences in plain language for executives explaining that the pilot slipped by two weeks because an upstream dependency delivered late, and that mitigation work is underway with a revised checkpoint next Friday. Keep the tone confident and calm, avoid jargon, and do not name individuals.","The pilot slipped two weeks because an upstream dependency delivered later than planned, which pushed our integration work. Mitigation is underway, and we will report progress at next Friday's checkpoint.\n\nNotice how blame stays off individuals\u2014Requirements named tone and \u201cno names,\u201d so the story stays executive-safe.","Executive-safe updates are engineered: audience, calm tone, two sentences, no villains\u2014most prompts skip at least one.","Jargon is a hiding place. If you do not forbid names and blame, the model will serve both\u2014then you look like you are throwing people under the bus.",B.ahV,B.Lm)
B.JJ=s([B.adE,B.adZ,B.aeI],t.r)
B.Hr=new A.bR("Expand or Shorten With Purpose",B.JJ,null)
