B.ahG=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five prompt elements that produce feature ideas as strategic bets\u2014not just a feature list.",B.Lt,"Your edge is forcing strategic fields (user/value/differentiator/risk/test). This stops \u201cfeature soup\u201d and produces bets you can actually evaluate.","Generate exactly 6 realistic feature/offer ideas. For each include target user, value proposition (1 sentence), differentiator, risk/trade-off, and a quick test. Don\u2019t invent market data; mark unknowns [Unknown]. Return only the list.","You\u2019re now using AI for strategy, not brainstorming theater\u2014ideas come with trade-offs and tests.","Generate exactly 6 realistic feature or offering ideas. For each include: Target user, Value proposition (1 sentence), Differentiator, Risk/Trade-off, Quick test. Do not invent market data; mark unknowns [Unknown]. Return only the list.")
B.a8G=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *strategic completeness without fake data*.\n- Requirements forced positioning elements (user/value/differentiator)\n- Risk/Trade-off prevents \u201conly upside\u201d thinking\n- Quick tests make ideas testable bets, not brainstorm wallpaper")
B.acK=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nGenerate feature ideas\n\nStrong prompt:\nGenerate exactly 6 realistic ideas. For each: target user, value proposition, differentiator, risk/trade-off, quick test. Don\u2019t invent market data; mark unknowns [Unknown]. Return only the list.")
B.a8b=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nNeed new offerings without inventing market reality\n\nO - Objective\nGenerate strategy-aligned ideas with validation paths\n\nR - Requirements\nUser/value/differentiator; risk/trade-off; quick test; no fake data\n\nE - Expectations\nExactly 6 ideas with the specified fields")
B.Kr=s([B.a8G,B.acK,B.a8b],t.c)
B.adS=new A.ab("Brainstorm new features or offerings","You want fresh ideas for a product or service but don\u2019t know where to start.\n\nThe risk: \u201cfeature lists\u201d are easy\u2014coherent strategy isn\u2019t.\n\nIf ideas ignore positioning, they won\u2019t sell.\n\nIf ideas ignore feasibility, they won\u2019t ship.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - product ideas under constraints\n- Objective - generate features aligned to a strategic hypothesis\n- Requirements - include target user, value proposition, and risk; no invented market facts\n- Expectations - ideas with differentiation + trade-offs + a test","Generate new feature or offering ideas.\n\nRequirements:\n- Provide exactly 6 ideas\n- For each idea include: Target user, Value proposition (1 sentence), Differentiator, Risk/Trade-off, Quick test\n- Keep ideas realistic (no magical capabilities)\n- Do not invent market data; mark unknowns [Unknown]\n\nReturn only the list.","- Quick-start templates for new users\n  - Target user: new users\n  - Value proposition: reduce setup time by providing ready-to-use starting points\n  - Differentiator: templates tailored to common workflows\n  - Risk/Trade-off: may constrain advanced users if templates become the default\n  - Quick test: release 3 templates and measure activation lift vs baseline [Unknown baseline]\n\n- Integrated analytics dashboard\n  - Target user: team leads\n  - Value proposition: make outcomes visible without exporting data\n  - Differentiator: decision-grade views with \u201cunknowns\u201d explicitly tagged\n  - Risk/Trade-off: complexity and maintenance cost\n  - Quick test: prototype top 3 metrics and validate with 5 power users\n\nNotice how this avoids \u201cidea soup\u201d: forcing user/value/differentiator/risk/test makes each feature a strategic bet with a validation path.","Strong strategy prompts turn ideas into testable bets.","If you don\u2019t force a risk/trade-off, you get fantasy features. Professionals treat ideas as bets with downsides and tests\u2014make the model do that work.",B.ahG,B.Kr)
B.ND=s([B.ael,B.adG,B.adS],t.r)
B.Ht=new A.bR("Generate Ideas Quickly",B.ND,null)
