B.ahP=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that make this a strong reusable prompt for escalation-ready task updates.",B.Nu,"Escalation-ready templates require risk field discipline and anti-invention constraints even when output is very short.","Create a reusable one- or two-sentence task update prompt with placeholders for task, status, risk, and next action; keep neutral and forbid invented progress claims.","You now have a compact update that scales upward without cleanup - most templates break at escalation.","Build a reusable 1-2 sentence task update prompt with placeholders for task, status, risk, and next action. Keep neutral, concise, and forward-safe.")
B.a8p=new A.k("What Made This Work","The difference is escalation fields: short templates still need risk discipline.\n- Objective includes status plus risk signal\n- Requirements lock concise neutral format\n- Expectations keep forwarding safety")
B.ac4=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nCreate a quick task template\n\nStrong prompt:\nCreate a reusable one- or two-sentence task update prompt with placeholders for task name, current status, risk level, and next action. Keep tone neutral and professional, forbid invented progress claims, and make output suitable for forwarding to leadership without reformatting.")
B.a8v=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nConcise task updates that may escalate upward\n\nO - Objective\nReport status, risk, and next action clearly\n\nR - Requirements\nOne or two sentences; neutral tone; required placeholders\n\nE - Expectations\nForward-safe reusable update line")
B.Nj=s([B.a8p,B.ac4,B.a8v],t.c)
B.ads=new A.ab("Create a Reusable Task Update Prompt for Escalation Readiness","You send frequent task updates that may be forwarded upward when risk increases. You need a reusable template prompt that stays concise but escalation-ready.\n\nIf this is vague, the update escalates without the one line leadership needs to judge risk.\n\nIf the prompt is too simple, AI usually:\n- omits risk signal\n- uses casual language that does not travel well\n- varies structure across tasks\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- no clear Objective\n- weak Requirements\n- no defined Expectations\n\nMost people template status but not escalation readiness.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - concise task updates that may escalate\n- Objective - report status, risk level, and next step clearly\n- Requirements - one or two sentences; neutral tone; required placeholders\n- Expectations - reusable line safe for cross-level forwarding","Create a reusable one- or two-sentence task update prompt with placeholders for task name, current status, risk level, and next action. Keep tone neutral and professional, forbid invented progress claims, and make output suitable for forwarding to leadership without reformatting.","Task Update Template\n[Task name] - Status: [status]. Risk: [risk level]. Next action: [next action].\n\nWhat matters here is the risk field - it is what makes a short update escalation-ready.","If a status template cannot survive escalation, it is not a template - it is a draft.","Most AI users stay average here: they report status but hide risk, then escalation arrives with missing context.",B.ahP,B.Nj)
B.KC=s([B.ae1,B.adl,B.ads],t.r)
B.Hv=new A.bR("Create Reusable Prompts for Daily Work",B.KC,u.k)
