B.aiq=new A.ac("Choose the five prompt elements that diagnose timeline slippage with plan-vs-actual evidence.",B.K9,"Under pressure, teams guess. Your advantage is forcing variance evidence so the conversation stays credible and actionable.","Rewrite into a diagnostic question about timeline slippage. Don\u2019t invent causes. Ask for plan vs actual breakdown by phase/step and top variance drivers with evidence needed. Output one question + breakdown structure.","You\u2019re now asking timeline questions that stay credible under scrutiny\u2014this is an operator-level advantage.","Rewrite the timeline concern into a diagnostic question. Do not invent causes. Require plan vs actual variance breakdown by phase/step. Ask for top candidate drivers with the evidence needed to confirm each. Output: one question plus the breakdown structure.")
B.a8g=new A.k("What Made This Work","The control point is *variance discipline*.\n- Requirements forced plan vs actual breakdown\n- Expectations demanded drivers + evidence (not opinions)\n- Objective kept it credible under pressure: isolate where slippage accumulates first")
B.aal=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nWhy are we behind schedule?\n\nStrong prompt:\nRewrite into a diagnostic question. Don\u2019t invent causes. Ask for plan vs actual breakdown by phase/step and top variance drivers with evidence needed. Output one question + breakdown structure.")
B.aaa=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nTimeline slipping; pressure for answers\n\nO - Objective\nIsolate where variance accumulates and why (evidence)\n\nR - Requirements\nNo invention; plan vs actual; variance drivers + evidence\n\nE - Expectations\nOne question + variance breakdown structure")
B.NI=s([B.a8g,B.aal,B.aaa],t.c)
B.adn=new A.ab("Turn timeline concerns into diagnostic questions","A delivery timeline is slipping and stakeholders want answers.\n\nIf you guess causes, you lose credibility.\n\nIf you stay vague, you lose trust.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - timeline slippage with uncertainty\n- Objective - diagnostic question that isolates where slippage accumulates\n- Requirements - compare plan vs actual; identify variance drivers; no invented causes\n- Expectations - one question + variance breakdown request","Rewrite the timeline concern into a diagnostic question.\n\nRequirements:\n- Do not invent causes\n- Ask for plan vs actual variance breakdown by phase/step\n- Ask for the top 3 variance drivers with evidence needed\n- Output: one question + the breakdown structure\n\nReturn only the output.","**Diagnostic question**\nWhere is timeline variance accumulating (which phase/step), and what evidence-based drivers explain the variance (scope change, rework, waiting, capacity)?\n\n**Breakdown structure**\n- Plan vs actual duration by phase/step\n- Variance contribution by phase (top contributors)\n- Top 3 candidate drivers + evidence to confirm each\n\nThe difference is variance discipline: the prompt forces plan-vs-actual breakdown so the analysis doesn\u2019t become a blame story.","Credible timeline analysis starts with variance, not opinions.","Schedule questions fail when they start with blame. Force plan-vs-actual variance first; then ask for evidence-based drivers.",B.aiq,B.NI)
