B.ae3=new A.ab("Build a Reusable Document Handoff Email",'You send the same kind of email whenever you share a policy draft: greeting, what the file is, what you need back, and by when.\n\nIf you say "make a template," AI often:\n- writes a one-off essay\n- forgets placeholders\n- hides the ask\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- no clear Objective\n- weak Requirements\n- no defined Expectations\n\nMost people get a pretty paragraph\u2014not a skeleton\u2014because they never demanded placeholders and reuse.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - internal email; policy draft handoff\n- Objective - share file; request review feedback\n- Requirements - placeholders for names and dates; two or three short paragraphs; professional tone\n- Expectations - reusable whenever a new draft ships',"Create a reusable email template for sharing a policy draft internally. Include placeholders for recipient name, document title, version date, and feedback deadline. Use two or three short paragraphs with a professional tone, state what review you need, and keep optional lines for attaching links versus files.","Subject: [Document title] \u2014 review requested (v[version date])\n\nHi [Name],\n\nI am sharing the [document title] for your review. The draft reflects [one-line purpose or scope].\n\nPlease send comments by [feedback deadline]. If you prefer, I can walk through questions on a short call.\n\nThank you,\n[Your Name]\n\nNotice how the slots are visible\u2014Requirements forced placeholders, so the output stays reusable instead of bespoke.","Reusable beats clever: slots, tone, and a reuse goal\u2014then you ship faster than people rewriting from scratch every week.","If your template does not embarrass you with brackets, it is probably a one-off dressed up as process.",B.aiU,B.Ku)
