B.aiv=new A.ac("C.O.R.E. skill check: choose the five elements that make this a strong prompt for a customer onboarding checklist template with ordered steps and owner placeholders.",B.Oo,"Checklist templates need ordered steps, owner slots, and rules against invented data.","Create a numbered onboarding checklist template with owner placeholders, no fake customer data, at most eight steps, and reusable for every new account.","Clean win: template prompts fail when \u201cmerge\u201d replaces limits\u2014your picks show you know how to cap structure and data.","Build an eight-step onboarding checklist template\u2014numbered, owner placeholders in brackets, no sample data, reusable for every new account.")
B.a8D=new A.k("What Made This Work","This is what changes the output: merged ideas need architecture, not enthusiasm.\n- Objective is a repeatable weekly shape\n- Requirements cap sections and ban numeric examples\n- Expectations demand scan speed, not essay density")
B.aaH=new A.k("Weak vs Strong Prompt","Weak prompt:\nMerge these ideas\n\nStrong prompt:\nDesign a weekly project snapshot template with at most four labeled sections covering progress, KPI focus, risks, and asks. Use bracket placeholders only, keep instructions under the headings minimal, and do not insert numeric examples. Make it easy to scan in under thirty seconds.")
B.a89=new A.k("C.O.R.E. Breakdown","C - Context\nWeekly snapshot for busy readers\n\nO - Objective\nStandardize reporting structure\n\nR - Requirements\nFour sections max; placeholders; no fake numbers\n\nE - Expectations\nScannable template")
B.Ol=s([B.a8D,B.aaH,B.a89],t.c)
B.adQ=new A.ab("Merge Rough Ideas Into One Scannable Template",'People dumped ideas into a doc:\n- "needs KPI section"\n- "maybe risks?"\n- "not too long"\n- "finance wants numbers"\n\nYou need one weekly project template everyone can reuse.\n\nIf you prompt "combine," AI often:\n- adds random sections\n- writes example numbers\n- loses the length cap\n\nThis is why your prompt fails:\n- no clear Objective\n- weak Requirements\n- no defined Expectations\n\n\u201cCombine\u201d is how you get fake KPIs\u2014because nobody banned sample data.\n\nTo get a usable result, your prompt must define:\n- Context - weekly project snapshot for cross-functional readers\n- Objective - progress, KPI focus, risks, asks\n- Requirements - max four sections; bracket placeholders only; no sample figures\n- Expectations - paste-ready template',"Design a weekly project snapshot template with at most four labeled sections covering progress, KPI focus, risks, and asks. Use bracket placeholders only, keep instructions under the headings minimal, and do not insert numeric examples. Make it easy to scan in under thirty seconds.","**[Project name] \u2014 Week of [date]**\n\n**Progress**\n- [3 bullets max]\n\n**KPI focus**\n- [Metric name] \u2014 [status vs target] \u2014 [note]\n\n**Risks**\n- [Risk] \u2014 [impact] \u2014 [mitigation owner]\n\n**Asks**\n- [What you need] \u2014 [from whom] \u2014 [by when]\n\nNotice how numbers never appear\u2014Expectations banned examples, so finance gets slots, not fiction.","Scannable beats complete: cap sections, ban sample numbers, force placeholders\u2014then you own the template, not the model\u2019s filler.","Templates balloon when section limits are missing\u2014the model adds sections because it thinks more looks thorough.",B.aiv,B.Ol)
